From: SORABBYNGO Engineering <kernel@sorabbyngo.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0011] lsm: sorabbyngo Linux Security Module

Implements a Sorabbyngo-specific LSM that sits alongside SELinux/AppArmor
in the LSM stacking framework (CONFIG_LSM="sorabbyngo,selinux,bpf").

The Sorabbyngo LSM enforces:

  1. NodeID-based process identity: every process spawned from a
     Sorabbyngo service inherits a NodeID label. Cross-node IPC
     (via Byngonet) is only allowed between processes with matching
     NodeID labels or explicitly authorised pairs.

  2. File integrity enforcement: executables in /opt/sorabbyngo/ must
     have a valid IMA (Integrity Measurement Architecture) measurement.
     Tampered binaries are blocked at execve() time.

  3. Byngonet socket restriction: AF_INET sockets bound to port 7422
     may only be created by processes with the BYNGONET_PEER label.
     Prevents rogue processes from impersonating Byngonet nodes.

  4. CML enforcement: any process calling the Anthropic API (outbound
     to api.anthropic.com) must pass through the CML NATS subject
     sorabbyngo.cml.filter.request. Direct outbound HTTPS to the
     Anthropic API without CML is blocked at the socket level.

  5. Audit trail: every LSM denial is written to the Sorabbyngo
     SHA-256 chained audit log in addition to standard audit(7).

Registered as a stacked LSM — does not replace SELinux.
